Stage: DB

Purpose:
  Database stage. Owns schema and data changes required by a unit of
  work — migrations, schema changes, seed/reference data, indexing —
  everything a later stage needs the data layer to already provide
  before it can build on top of it.


Requires:
  none (DB is typically the entry point of a chain when data changes
  are part of the unit of work — see chains.sdd -> ParallelExample,
  where DB has no upstream dependency)


Produces:
  Applied/reviewed schema or data change that downstream stages (BE,
  API) can rely on as a stable contract.


Blocks:
  BE, API — when the unit of work includes a data-layer change, BE/API
  MUST NOT execute until this stage is DONE (see chains.sdd -> Rules
  [C5]).


Optional:
  This stage is skipped (never silently — see chains.sdd -> Rules [C7])
  when the unit of work introduces no schema or data change.


Skills:
  @../../skills/database/

  (see chains.sdd -> DoesNotOwn — this file defines WHEN/responsibility
  only; HOW the schema/data change is actually implemented belongs to
  skills/database/, not here.)


State: + (vocabulary defined here; skills/database/ content is not yet
  written — see skills/skills.sdd -> SkillDomains, state: boş)


Note:
  (prompt/new/33.md, STEP 11) Extracted out of the flat feature.chain /
  bugfix.chain / change.chain, where the DB responsibility was repeated
  inline in each file. Defined once here per NoDuplication; referenced
  from chains.sdd -> Stages and from every template under ./templates/
  that includes a DB step.
